---
description: REST API conventions for the backend.
alwaysApply: true
---

# API Design

Follow REST principles.

Base URL

/api/v1

---

# Naming

Good

/users

/reservations

/memberships

/menu-items

Bad

/getUsers

/createReservation

---

# HTTP Methods

GET

POST

PUT

PATCH

DELETE

Use them correctly.

---

# Responses

Always return consistent JSON.

Example

{
  "success": true,
  "message": "",
  "data": {},
  "meta": {}
}

---

# Errors

Example

{
  "success": false,
  "message": "Reservation not found",
  "errors": []
}

---

# Pagination

Support:

page

limit

sort

order

search

---

# Filtering

Prefer query parameters.

Never create unnecessary endpoints.

---

# Status Codes

200

201

204

400

401

403

404

409

422

500

Use appropriately.

---

# Authentication

Bearer Token.

Never use cookies unless explicitly required.

---

# Versioning

Always support:

/api/v1

Future:

/api/v2

---

# Documentation

Every endpoint must appear in OpenAPI.

No undocumented endpoints.